<GuideLayout
  title="Privacy policy of this Canadian salary calculator 2026"
  description="Your salary, province and pay frequency stay in your browser. Canada Net Pay sets no cookies and keeps no personal information; only site stability is checked."
  publishDate="2026-06-27"
  modifiedDate="2026-10-06"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <p><em>Last updated: October 6, 2026</em> · <a href="/fr/confidentialite/" hreflang="fr" lang="fr">Version française</a></p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <p>
    Canada Net Pay is a static website published by {LEGAL.entityName}. It sets no cookies, and its
    publisher collects and keeps no personal information about you. This policy is written with the
    federal <em>Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act</em> (PIPEDA) in mind and,
    for visitors in Quebec, the <em>Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private
    sector</em> as amended by Law 25.
  </p>

  <h2>What you type into the calculators</h2>
  <p>
    Gross salary, province or territory, pay frequency, RRSP contributions, CPP or OAS figures: whatever you
    enter to estimate take-home pay, income tax, CPP, EI or Old Age Security is computed by JavaScript on
    your own device. None of it is sent to a server, stored in a database or saved on your device; closing
    the tab erases it. When you share a link to a result, the amount and province travel in the part of the
    address after the <code>#</code>, which browsers never send to the server.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    No cookie is set by canadanetpay.com, by its calculators or by the stability tool described below, and
    nothing is written to your browser’s local or session storage. There is therefore no cookie banner:
    nothing has to be accepted or declined. The site carries no advertising and no advertising or social
    media trackers.
  </p>

  <h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2>
  <p>
    To spot what breaks (script errors, slow loading, buttons that do not respond to clicks, odd scrolling),
    the site runs <strong>Microsoft Clarity in cookieless mode</strong>. In this mode Clarity writes none of
    the cookies <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>. Every page view
    gets its own identifier, so two page views, or two visits, are never tied together. The text of the
    page and the figures you type are masked in your browser before anything leaves it: Microsoft never
    sees your salary or your province.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Who processes it</strong>: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland. The data may be processed outside Canada, including in the United States; see <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Why</strong>: a technical, anonymous check that the pay and pension calculators load and compute correctly.</li>
    <li><strong>How long</strong>: page-view recordings are deleted after 30 days, aggregated figures after 13 months.</li>
    <li><strong>On what basis</strong>: the publisher’s legitimate interest in a calculator that works, a purpose a reasonable person would consider appropriate (PIPEDA, s. 5(3)); for visitors from the European Union, Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR.</li>
    <li><strong>How to opt out</strong>: block <code>clarity.ms</code> in your browser or content blocker (every calculator works the same without it), or write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc.). Like any web server, it records technical details of
    each request, such as IP address, time, page requested and browser, to keep the service secure and
    running. The publisher cannot see these logs and makes no use of them.
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    A message sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or through the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> is used only to reply. Your address is not put on a mailing list or
    shared with anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Under PIPEDA and Quebec’s Law 25 you may ask what information is held about you and have it corrected.
    Since the publisher keeps none, this in practice concerns only messages you have sent us; for stability
    monitoring you can also contact Microsoft. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the
    {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">report a concern</a>)
    or, in Quebec, to the Commission d’accès à l’information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If the way the site works changes, this page is updated first and the date at the top moves forward.
  </p>
  <OfficialSources />
</GuideLayout>
